@host = http://localhost:5041

### All tickets (10)
GET {{host}}/tickets

### One ticket
GET {{host}}/tickets/1

### Missing ticket -> 404
GET {{host}}/tickets/999

### Open tickets, highest priority first
GET {{host}}/tickets/open

### The SQL EF generates for that query, without running it
GET {{host}}/tickets/sql?status=Open

### Status from the query string, no hardcoded "Open" in the repository
GET {{host}}/tickets?status=Open

### Two filters combined
GET {{host}}/tickets?status=Open&minPriority=3

### The SQL for two filters — note the parameters
GET {{host}}/tickets/sql?status=Open&minPriority=3

### Counted by the database, not in C#
GET {{host}}/tickets/open/count

### Priority 4 and up, newest first
GET {{host}}/tickets/high-priority

### Ticket plus customer, one round trip (Include)
GET {{host}}/tickets/1/with-customer

### Variant B: same rows, fetched the slow way — no WHERE in the SQL log
GET {{host}}/tickets/high-priority/in-memory

### Database filter, then AsEnumerable, then a C# filter EF cannot translate
GET {{host}}/tickets/open/title?word=log

### Missing word -> 400
GET {{host}}/tickets/open/title

### Del 7: open tickets with a title longer than 15 chars (C#-side filter)
GET {{host}}/tickets/open/long-title

### Oppgave 5: every ticket with its customer (Include)
GET {{host}}/tickets/with-customer

### Oppgave 6: projection straight to a DTO - five columns, no Include
GET {{host}}/tickets/summary

### Oppgave 7: the same data via Include - ten columns
GET {{host}}/tickets/summary/via-include

### Del 15: open only, priority down then oldest first
GET {{host}}/tickets/summary/open

### Del 16-17: filters applied only when sent
GET {{host}}/tickets/summary?status=Open&minPriority=3

### Del 18: the SQL for each filter combination
GET {{host}}/tickets/summary/sql

###
GET {{host}}/tickets/summary/sql?status=Open

###
GET {{host}}/tickets/summary/sql?minPriority=3

###
GET {{host}}/tickets/summary/sql?status=Open&minPriority=3

### Oppgave 13: WHERE, ORDER BY and TOP done by the database
GET {{host}}/tickets/top-open?count=5

### Oppgave 10: one query, every customer, zero included
GET {{host}}/customers/ticket-counts

### Del 19-21: the same answer as N+1 - count the SELECTs in the log
GET {{host}}/customers/ticket-counts/n-plus-one

### Oppgave 11: Any becomes EXISTS
GET {{host}}/customers/with-open-tickets

### Del 26: HasOpenTickets computed by the database
GET {{host}}/customers/statuses

### Del 28: a customer and their tickets, one query
GET {{host}}/customers/1/tickets

### Missing customer -> 404
GET {{host}}/customers/999/tickets

### Utfordring 1: customers with at least 2 tickets, busiest first
GET {{host}}/customers/busy?minTickets=2

### Utfordring 2: open tickets at priority 4+, oldest first
GET {{host}}/tickets/important

### Bonus: a read-only query with change tracking off
GET {{host}}/tickets/open/no-tracking
